Got it, if add slotId as a parameter to hostStatusCallback, then activate() will be called if slotId == sensor->slotId. Did I understand correctly?
Besides, there's a judgement in activate() to avoid repetition.
```
void PSUSensor::activate()
{
    if (isActive())
    {
        // Avoid activating an active sensor
        return;
    }

    inputDev.open(path, boost::asio::random_access_file::read_only);
    markAvailable(true);
    setupRead();
}
```

